# User Flows

Greek learning app with SRS-based vocabulary practice and timed production drills.

## Quick Reference

Generated from `src/routeTree.gen.ts`. The practice drills are not listed here —
they are owned by the per-group catalogues (see **Practice** below), and any list
kept in this file would drift from them.

```
/                          Dashboard (home)
/login  /register          Sign in (password or passkey) · create account
/try                       Anonymous drill, 8 prompts: 6 pronouns plus θέλω, έχω (conversion flow)

/practice                  Drill browser, a four-row list of groups
/practice/cases            Case drills, sectioned Doer · Target · Owner · Review
/practice/pronouns         Object forms, placement, possessives
/practice/verbs            Present · Past · Future & Modal · Mixed tenses
/practice/blocks           Survival phrases, numbers, days, opposites
/practice/blocks/question-words   ποιος / πόσος agreement, own sub-index
/practice/review           Drills gone rusty, grouped by category

/learn                     Learn landing (SectionIndex)
/learn/conversations/:tab  Themed dialogues
/learn/phrases/:tab        Common expressions
/learn/nouns  /:subject    Noun browser by subject
/learn/verbs  /:verbId     Verb browser · full conjugation detail
/learn/essentials/:subtab  Numbers, colours, time, position, frequency

/reference                 Reference landing (SectionIndex)
/reference/:tab            Grammar reference by topic
/reference/verbs  /:band   Verb reference, by tense band

/search                    Vocabulary search
/progress                  Analytics (streak calendar, accuracy trends)
/support                   About page

/api/errors                Client error log (POST), called by the error pages
/api/webauthn/*            register-options · register-verify · auth-options · auth-verify
```

## Routes

### Practice

Every drill route is thin: it owns its item data and hands it to `<Drill>` with a
`drillId`. Everything else about the drill — its name, its route, the sample forms
and estimated minutes shown in a list, its category and case role — lives in one
catalogue entry:

<catalogue>
<file>src/routes/practice/cases/drills.data.ts</file>
<file>src/routes/practice/verbs/drills.data.ts</file>
<file>src/routes/practice/pronouns/drills.data.ts</file>
<file>src/routes/practice/blocks/drills.data.ts</file>
<file>src/routes/practice/blocks/question-words/drills.data.ts</file>
<derived>src/routes/practice/drill-catalogue.data.ts — the by-id lookup, flattened from the above</derived>
<guard>src/routes/practice/drill-catalogue.test.ts — fails if a drill and the catalogue disagree</guard>
</catalogue>

Read those files for the current drill list. A drill's `caseRole` also decides its
colour: `doer`/`target`/`owner` take the reserved case tokens, `mixed` and `null`
take the base palette and claim nothing.

<route path="/practice">
<purpose>Drill browser: a four-row list, one row per group</purpose>
<file>src/routes/practice/index.tsx</file>
<note>An auth guard on practice/route.tsx redirects logged-out visitors to /</note>
</route>

<route path="/practice/{cases,verbs,pronouns,blocks}">
<purpose>Per-group drill index</purpose>
<file>src/routes/practice/&lt;group&gt;/index.tsx</file>
<data-source>That group's drills.data.ts</data-source>
<displays>Drill rows (title, sample Greek, minutes), sectioned by phase where the group has phases</displays>
</route>

<route path="/practice/review">
<purpose>Drills that have gone rusty, grouped by category</purpose>
<file>src/routes/practice/review.tsx</file>
<data-source>DB: getSchemaRust(userId), filtered against the drill catalogue</data-source>
<displays>Rust bar per drill, days since last practice, recent accuracy</displays>
</route>

### Dashboard and auth

<route path="/">
<purpose>Dashboard — primary entry point</purpose>
<file>src/routes/index.tsx</file>
<data-source>DB: vocabProgress / drillProgress via the dashboard server fns</data-source>
<displays>
- Contextual practice CTA: first-time, all-caught-up, lapsed, or rusty drills.
  The rusty-drills CTA reads "N drills to review" and lists up to three, each
  with how rusty it is and days since last practice. No time estimate.
- Weekly streak grid (Mon-Sun) and freeze indicator
- Mastered / learning counts
</displays>
<note>Logged-out visitors get LandingPage here instead of the dashboard</note>
</route>

<route path="/login">
<purpose>Sign in — password or passkey</purpose>
<file>src/routes/(auth)/login.tsx</file>
<user-actions>
- Username + password
- Username without a password (existing accounts) → prompted to set one
- Passkey via WebAuthn
</user-actions>
</route>

<route path="/register">
<purpose>Account creation, with optional passkey setup after</purpose>
<file>src/routes/(auth)/register.tsx</file>
</route>

<route path="/try">
<purpose>Anonymous drill for try-before-signup</purpose>
<file>src/routes/try.tsx</file>
<data-source>Static: 8 hardcoded prompts, 6 pronouns (each with a hint line) plus θέλω and έχω</data-source>
<displays>
- Intro: prompt count, 6 seconds a prompt (medium speed), Greeklish explained
- The drill, ending on the drill's SummaryScreen with an account pitch below it
  ("Create a free account", "Sign in")
</displays>
<note>The only drill with no catalogue entry; it passes its own title to &lt;Drill&gt;</note>
</route>

### Learn and reference

<route path="/learn">
<purpose>SectionIndex into conversations, phrases, nouns, verbs, essentials: a ruled, Greek-first list with no icons or tints. /reference and /learn/essentials use the same component.</purpose>
